{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And these words.</b> The unification and the love that were mentioned shall be engraved upon your hearts — or they are the commandments that are in the Torah. <b>Which I command you this day.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: let the commandments not be in your eyes like an old edict (diyotigma) that no one pays heed to, but like a new edict that everyone rushes to read; so too ״which I command you this day״ — let them be in your eyes as new as though you received them today from Sinai. A diyotigma is a royal decree that comes in writing."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:45:57.173013543Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}